  "interpretation": [
    "The lower-error outline checkpoint passes curve geometry but fails the guarded paper-core test at 360, 700, 1000 and 1400 cells. This is not cured by finer verification.",
    "Both failures are mirrored portions of one short hook on paper A. At resolution 1000 each detached possible-core component occupies 0.94 mm squared. The actual paper need not be disconnected: it is the prescribed-width disk-centre core that fails.",
    "The captured automatic settings exclude same-slit force samples within eight nominal widths (20.040 mm), not the general default of three. A close pair near the hook is 12.249 mm apart along the path and 2.426 mm apart spatially, below the 2.505 mm nominal width. Reducing the force exclusion to three widths (7.515 mm) addresses this otherwise ignored region without changing the independent acceptance rules.",
    "The proposed penalty change leaves validation, source masks, deadlines and final acceptance untouched; fixed-work evidence alone does not establish broader reliability."
  ],
